  "description": "Certificate of Lawful develoment for proposed works comprise selected replacement windows and external doors, including new front door, new garage doors, replacement of the roof and window to the existing garden shed, the installation of 2 no. air source heat pumps in the garden, and  installation of solar photo voltaic.\rProposed window and door works relate to an existing single dwellinghouse to replace existing windows and doors with new high-performance units in corresponding locations. The replacement units  to maintain an appropriate domestic appearance and to be sympathetic to the existing house and conservation area setting.  Create a new dwelling, or change the use of the property.\rReplacement front door forms part of the same programme of domestic repair, maintenance and energy-improvement works. Its detailed design, material and finish are to be selected to sit appropriately within the existing front elevation and the wider streetscape. Existing grp garage door is to be replaced with new hinged painted timber boarded doors.\rProposed repairs to the existing garden shed in the south-east corner of the property serve to improve an existing amenity that is used for purposes incidental to the enjoyment of the dwellinghouse. It will not be used as independent residential accommodation, commercial accommodation or any separate planning unit. Its footprint, height, location and materials will remain as shown on the accompanying drawings.  Proposed that 2 no. air source heat pumps be located in the rear garden 1m from the boundary and 8m from the adjacent house at no. 6 Frank Dixon Way. The installation will meet the permitted development rights including compliance with the Microgeneration Certification Scheme Planning Standards; total volume not exceeding 1.5m3; a sound power level of 60dB(A).\r\r",
